_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 59
---
order: 59
---
short_label: X.59
---
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and the sixth binomial, then the side of the area is the irrational straight line called the side of the sum of two medial areas.
---
proof:

Let the area *ABCD* be contained by the rational straight line *AB* and the sixth binomial *AD*, divided into its terms at *E*, so that *AE* is the greater term.

I say that the side of *AC* is the side of the sum of two medial areas.

Make the same construction as shown before.

It is then clear that *MO* is the side of *AC*, and that *MN* is incommensurable in square with *NO*.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="400" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.59 diagram" src="propX54.gif"/></noscript>
